  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      52.2,
      199.7,
      551.69,
      283.18
    ],
    "text": "The Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development has conducted a series of training and awareness programs to facilitate the adoption of e-Procurement in Sri Lanka. Joining the list of countries that facilitate e-Procurement, Sri Lanka had the opportunity to learn from international experience, adopt proven approaches and accelerate towards a modern, transparent and data-driven public procurement system. Why e-GP Matters",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.039999961853027,
      18.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      46.8,
      290.69,
      557.21,
      726.14
    ],
    "text": "e-GP enhances transparency and accountability, reduces administrative burdens, improves procurement efficiency and supplier access, strengthens electronic records, and provides reliable procurement data for better analysis and decision-making.",
